Backport of triton-lang/triton 2ddb39586b ("[SM120] Fallback MN-packed FP4 MMA
to the decomposition path", #10726), which lands after the revision pinned in
third_party/triton/workspace.bzl.

sm120's block-scaled MMA requires K-packed operands. ScaledBlockedToMMA does not
check that for fp4xfp4, so an MN-packed fp4 operand reaches
mma.sync.m16n8k64.mxf4nvf4 and is miscompiled rather than declined -- the packed
K-elements land on the wrong lanes. Measured on an RTX 5090 with a K=128 dot
whose operands both carry v_k = (k even ? 1 : 2) and unit block scales, so the
correct result is sum_k v_k^2 = 320: XLA's canonical rhs ([K,N], contracting=0)
gives 288 under ExperimentalTiling and aborts under SymbolicTiling.

XLA reaches this because a canonical rhs makes K the major dimension, so
dot_algorithms.cc sets rhs_k_pack=false, which faithfully describes the layout:

  tt.dot_scaled ... {fastMath = true, rhs_k_pack = false}
    : tensor<16x64xi8>, ... * tensor<128x8xi8>, ...

Declining sends it to DecomposeScaledBlocked, which upcasts to bf16 and is
correct. Note this is deliberately NARROW: K-packed fp4xfp4 is fine on sm120 --
verified against both this pinned revision and upstream main with a native
Triton kernel, and every other fp4 golden probe passes on the native path --
so a blanket fp4xfp4 decline would give up working W4A4 tensor-core throughput.

DELETE THIS when the pin moves past 2ddb39586b. Bumping was tried and reverted:
tmemfix.patch, an unrelated CUDA 12.8/13.2 TMEM shim, no longer applies across
that range.

